PLACEHOLDER - NOT THE ACTUAL BINARY

This file is a stand-in for the Antarctica thermal overlay mesh (COLLADA).
The real binary lives in upstream as a Git LFS object (~201 MB).

Upstream reference:
  Repository : https://github.com/dipraj-debnath/ROS2_MultiUAV_3D
  Path       : aerostack_examples/02_examples_gazebo_project/project_gazebo/models/aspa135_mini3_thermal_overlay/meshes/thermal_plane.dae
  LFS OID    : 3c5d16d218cf42ffb15cefb6ab481d3ede79543a3df281ab0a5ff2b1b1d8e64b (sha-256)
  LFS bytes  : 211493406

To restore the real thermal overlay mesh:
  git clone https://github.com/dipraj-debnath/ROS2_MultiUAV_3D /tmp/upstream
  cd /tmp/upstream && git lfs install && git lfs pull
  cp /tmp/upstream/aerostack_examples/02_examples_gazebo_project/project_gazebo/models/aspa135_mini3_thermal_overlay/meshes/thermal_plane.dae <repo>/aerostack_examples/02_examples_gazebo_project/project_gazebo/models/aspa135_mini3_thermal_overlay/meshes/

After restoring, re-enable LFS tracking in .gitattributes if you intend to
re-commit it (see .gitattributes for the line to add).
